Why this is here
----------------

A workshop item for a paid application can be fetched only by an account
that owns that application, and the only interface Valve offers for doing so
is the Steamworks SDK, which is proprietary. Without this permission the GPL
would forbid distributing WallFlux linked against it, and every wallpaper
somebody wanted would mean a trip to the Steam client by hand.

What it does not cover
----------------------

The Steamworks SDK and nothing else. Every other library WallFlux links has
to be compatible with the GNU General Public License as before, and the
Steamworks SDK's own licence still applies to the Steamworks SDK.
